Context: Ontology designers can attach SWRL business rules to a class in
Studio. Builders then run a rule on one entity from the Graph Explorer
(confirmation modal) or through a new MCP tool (no confirmation). The rule
runs scoped to that entity, the inferred triples are materialised into the
graph, and the Explorer canvas refreshes. Candidate rules are those whose
atoms cite the class or one of its parent classes. The Cypher translator
(Neo4j) is still scaffolding, so Neo4j domains infer no facts.

