## Fix decision table semantics: optional columns, Unique hit policy, Assign entity

Context: Three DecisionTableEngine behaviours contradicted the editor:
(1) every input column was INNER JOINed, so an instance missing any column
attribute never matched, even where its cell was "any"; a condition on a
column without an attribute referenced an alias that was never joined;
(2) the "unique" hit policy behaved like "all"; (3) the "Assign entity"
output action was ignored, so nothing was inferred.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/reasoning/DecisionTableEngine.py
   build_violation_sql LEFT JOINs only the columns used by an active
   condition and skips conditions on columns without an attribute.
   Per-row execution collects matches per instance, then applies the hit
   policy: first (first row), all (every row), unique (several rows ->
   conflict violation, no output). New ASSIGN_CLASS output: _resolve_dt
   resolves the class named in output value / row action values and the
   engine infers rdf:type triples. Output emission factored into _emit /
   _describe_output. validate_table requires an entity for Assign entity.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/OntologyRules.py
   decision_table_reference_errors flags unknown classes assigned by an
   assign_class output.
3. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html
   Output row reordered (action first); new "Entity to assign" select shown
   for Assign entity; Hit Policy, grid and output help texts describe the
   new behaviour.
4. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js
   Editor loads/saves assign_class as {property: "", action, value: class};
   _dtSyncOutputValue toggles property/value vs entity fields;
   dtDescribeTable describes Assign entity ("typed as X") and Unique
   conflicts, drops the "has a value for" clause and the obsolete warning.
5. docs/features.md
   Decision Tables & Aggregate Rules entry.
6. tests/units/ontology/test_decision_table_semantics.py (new),
   tests/units/front/test_decision_table_editor_help.py
   Engine coverage (LEFT JOIN, skipped columns, first/all/unique, assign
   class default and per-row, validation, reference errors); editor
   expectations updated.

Browser check: desktop 1400px and mobile 400px; Assign entity save, reload
and delete round-trip OK; no console errors.

